LQS = [
    (('Define science? Describe how the nature of science makes it different from other modes of knowing?', 'سائنس کی تعریف کریں۔ بیان کریں کہ سائنس کی نوعیت اسے علم کے دوسرے طریقوں سے کیسے مختلف بناتی ہے؟', 'ساینس تعریف کړئ؟ بیان کړئ چې د ساینس طبیعت یې د پوهې له نورو لارو څنګه توپیري کوي؟'),
     'Science (Latin "scientia", to know) is an organized form of knowledge obtained by observation and experimentation; it is systematic, tested and brought under general principles. Every branch of knowledge has its own way of study; science uses the scientific method - collecting data, forming hypotheses and testing them by experiment. This systematic, testable approach to day-to-day problems makes it different from history, literature and other branches. Scientific knowledge is reliable yet tentative: it changes only through further inquiry, debate and evidence.'),
    (('Write the contribution of three famous scientists of Pakistan.', 'پاکستان کے تین مشہور سائنسدانوں کی خدمات لکھیں۔', 'د پاکستان د درېیو مشهورو ساینس پوهانو ونډه ولیکئ.'),
     'Dr. Abdus Salam (b.1926): Nobel Prize physicist who presented the theory unifying two of the four basic forces. Dr. Abdul Qadeer Khan (b.1936): nuclear scientist, expert in uranium enrichment; tested nuclear devices at Chaghi on 28 May 1998 and established Kahuta Research Laboratories (KRL). Dr. Ashfaq Ahmad Khan (b.1930): chairman of the Pakistan Atomic Energy Commission for 10 years, founded GCISC, awarded Nishan-i-Imtiaz. (Also: Dr. Munir Ahmad Khan - IAEA, PINSTECH; Dr. Samar Mubarak Mand - lasers, fiber optics, missile technology.)'),
    (('Muslims scientists made significant contributions in the field of Science. Write some of the prominent contributions of Jaber bin Hayyan, Bu-Ali-Sina and Ibn-ul-Haitham in the field of Science.', 'مسلمان سائنسدانوں نے سائنس میں نمایاں خدمات انجام دیں۔ جابر بن حیان، بو علی سینا اور ابن الہیثم کی نمایاں خدمات لکھیں۔', 'مسلمانو ساینس پوهانو په ساینس کې مهمه ونډه درلوده. د جابر بن حیان، بو علي سینا او ابن الهیثم مهمې ونډې ولیکئ.'),
     'Jaber bin Hayyan (722-817): father of chemistry; own laboratory; invented sulfuric, nitric and hydrochloric acids; defined chemical reactions as union of elements in tiny particles (ten centuries before Dalton); techniques of crystallization, distillation, sublimation and evaporation. Bu-Ali-Sina (980-1037): over 100 books; "Al-Qanoon Fil-Tib" taught in Europe till the 17th century; "Al-Shifa" on physics, chemistry, arithmetic, biology and music; first to describe meningitis, parts of the eye and heart valves; found that nerves cause perceived muscle pain. Ibn-ul-Haitham (965-1039): principles of reflection and refraction of light, work on lenses and the eye, "Kitab-Al-Manazir" translated into Latin; father of optics.'),
    (('Do you think The Holy Quran give due importance to the acquisition of knowledge and it compels its reader to ponder over the various processes and phenomena occurring in the universe. Support your answer by quoting some verses of The Holy Quran.', 'کیا آپ سمجھتے ہیں کہ قرآن مجید حصولِ علم کو مناسب اہمیت دیتا ہے اور قاری کو کائنات کے مختلف عوامل اور مظاہر پر غور کرنے پر آمادہ کرتا ہے؟ قرآن کی چند آیات سے اپنے جواب کی تائید کریں۔', 'آیا تاسو فکر کوئ چې قرآن کریم د پوهې ترلاسه کولو ته مناسب اهمیت ورکوي او لوستونکی د کایناتو په بهیرونو او پدیدو کې فکر ته هڅوي؟ د قرآن د ځینو آیتونو په راوړلو خپل ځواب ثابت کړئ.'),
     'Yes. The Quran lays great emphasis on knowledge and invites man to travel and search the hidden realities of the universe; the Prophet (PBUH) said that acquiring knowledge is the duty of every Muslim man and woman. Verses: Al-Baqarah 2:164 (signs in the creation of heavens and earth, alternation of night and day, ships, rain reviving dead earth, animals, winds and clouds "for a people that are wise"); Al-Imran 3:190-191 (the creation of earth and heavens and the difference of day and night are signs for the wise, who ponder over them); An-Nur 24:45 (Allah created every living thing from water - some crawl, some are four-legged, some two-legged).'),
    (('Give detail account of different branches of science and their interrelationship with each other.', 'سائنس کی مختلف شاخوں اور ان کے باہمی تعلق کا تفصیلی جائزہ پیش کریں۔', 'د ساینس د بېلابېلو څانګو او د هغوی د متقابلې اړیکې مفصل حال ولیکئ.'),
     'Science is pure (explains phenomena) or applied (puts them to use). Pure science: physical sciences (physics - time, light, gravity; chemistry - properties, composition, structure and reactions of matter; astronomy - universe beyond earth), earth sciences (geology, oceanography, meteorology, paleontology) and life sciences/biology (botany, genetics, zoology, medicine); mathematical science includes arithmetic, algebra, geometry and calculus. The branches overlap: light (physics) drives photosynthesis (chemistry) in plants (biology). Such overlaps create compound sciences such as biochemistry, biophysics, biostatistics and environmental chemistry.'),
    (('List down some of the important developments in the medical field which have provided relief to humanity.', 'طب کے شعبے کی چند اہم پیش رفت لکھیں جنہوں نے انسانیت کو راحت پہنچائی۔', 'په طب کې ځینې مهم پرمختګونه ولیکئ چې انسانیت ته یې ارامي ورکړې.'),
     'Vaccines and drugs controlling plague, cholera, typhoid, polio and pneumonia; eradication of smallpox (declared 8 May 1980); diagnostic tools - X-rays, sonography/ultrasound, biopsy; laser treatment of cancer cells and retina (microsurgery); repair of heart valves, bypass grafting and pacemakers; transplant of eye, heart, kidneys and lungs.'),
    (('What is the contribution of developments taken place in the field of agriculture and medicines for the welfare of mankind.', 'زراعت اور طب کے شعبوں میں ہونے والی ترقی نے انسانیت کی فلاح میں کیا حصہ ڈالا؟', 'د کرنې او طب په برخو کې پرمختګونو د انسانیت هوساینې ته څه ونډه ورکړې؟'),
     'Agriculture: modern machines (tractors, scrapers, harvesters, tube wells) made farming profitable and raised production; water logging and salinity were partly overcome and land reclaimed; tissue culture and genetic engineering produced disease- and drought-resistant, high-yield, pest-resistant crops, so food quality and quantity increased for a growing population. Medicine: vaccines and drugs controlled killer diseases, modern diagnosis (X-rays, sonography, biopsy), laser surgery, heart surgery and organ transplants made life healthier and more secure.'),
    (('Write some important contributions of Greek in the field of science.', 'سائنس کے میدان میں یونانیوں کی چند اہم خدمات لکھیں۔', 'په ساینس کې د یونانیانو ځینې مهمې ونډې ولیکئ.'),
     'In the Greek period (300-600 BC) Aristotle, Archimedes, Galen and Pythagoras contributed greatly. Greeks were the first to develop theories from observations; Pythagoras took a mathematical view of the world; Aristotle and Plato developed logical methods for examining the world; and the Greeks first suggested that matter is made of atoms - fundamental particles that cannot be broken down further.'),
]
